@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #264653
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 18
  BorderColor #264653
  FontColor #1F2933
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #264653
  FontColor #1F2933
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #264653
  FontColor #1F2933
}
left to right direction

actor "MFD author" as Author
actor "C++ integrator" as Integrator
actor "Runtime operator" as Operator

package "MFDStudio repository" {
  rectangle "assets/\nwindow, pages,\nreticles, images" as Assets #E9F5DB
  rectangle "mfd_editor\nvisual authoring" as Editor #D9EDFF
  rectangle "mfd_client_api/generator\nC++ UI + .generated.map" as Generator #FFF3D6
  rectangle "Client application\ncockpit-specific logic" as ClientApp #FFF3D6
  rectangle "mfd_window\nruntime + F1 overlay" as Runtime #FFE3E3
  rectangle "Framebuffer plugin\nstable DLL ABI" as Plugin #F3E8FF
}

Author --> Editor : design and save
Editor --> Assets : write authored model
Assets --> Generator : input source
Integrator --> Generator : configure generation
Generator --> ClientApp : emit generated headers / sources
Generator --> Assets : write <window>.generated.map
Integrator --> ClientApp : implement business logic
Operator --> ClientApp : provide live data
ClientApp --> Runtime : UDP protobuf commands
Runtime --> ClientApp : optional UDP feedback
Runtime --> Plugin : submit RGBA32 frames
Operator --> Runtime : observe rendered window

note bottom of Runtime
The runtime owns rendered scene state.
The client owns business data and publish cadence.
end note
@enduml
